  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1226 AM CDT Wed May 13 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will dominate the weather across West Central \nTexas through the end of the work week. This will result in hot and \ndry conditions across the region. Highs will be mostly be in the \n90s, with overnight lows in the 60s to near 70. The hottest day will \nbe Friday, in the upper 90s to near 104 across northwest portions of \nthe region. Most of the rest of the area will be in the low to mid \n90s. \n\nAs we head into the weekend and into early next week, a broad upper \nlevel trough will develop across the western CONUS. This will place \nWest Central Texas in southwest flow aloft. This will result in \nslightly cooler temperatures, albeit still well above normal. Highs \nwill generally be in the 90s to near 100. Diurnally driven showers \nand thunderstorms will be possible every afternoon, especially \nSunday into the beginning of next week, mainly along the dryline. \nThere remains quite a bit of uncertainty this far out, so for now \nhave kept PoPs in the low to medium range (20-50%).",
